msgid "Background"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:35
msgid ""
"Before you get started, familiarise yourself with what parameters are in "
"ROS: :doc:`../About-Parameters`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:38
msgid "Declaring parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:40
msgid ""
"By default, a node needs to *declare* all of the parameters that it will "
"accept during its lifetime. This is so that the type and name of the "
"parameters are well-defined at node startup time, which reduces the chances "
"of misconfiguration later on. See :doc:`../client-libraries/Working-with-"
"Client-Libraries/Using-Parameters-In-A-Class-CPP` or :doc:`../client-"
"libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Using-Parameters-In-A-Class-Python` "
"for tutorials on declaring and using parameters from a node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:44
msgid ""
"For some types of nodes, not all of the parameters will be known ahead of "
"time. In these cases, the node can be instantiated with "
"``allow_undeclared_parameters`` set to ``true``, which will allow parameters "
"to be get and set on the node even if they haven't been declared."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:48
msgid "Setting parameter types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:50
msgid ""
"Each parameter has one of the predefined parameter types listed in :doc:`../"
"About-Parameters`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:52
msgid ""
"By default, attempts to change the type of a declared parameter at runtime "
"will fail. This prevents common mistakes, such as putting a boolean value "
"into an integer parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:55
msgid ""
"If a parameter needs to be multiple different types, and the code using the "
"parameter can handle it, this default behavior can be changed. The parameter "
"should be declared using a ``ParameterDescriptor`` with the "
"``dynamic_typing`` member variable set to ``true``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:59
msgid "Interacting with parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:61
msgid ""
"ROS nodes can perform parameter operations using client libraries as "
"described in :doc:`../client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Using-"
"Parameters-In-A-Class-CPP` or :doc:`../client-libraries/Working-with-Client-"
"Libraries/Using-Parameters-In-A-Class-Python`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:63
msgid ""
