#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:89
msgid "Setting initial parameter values when launching nodes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:91
msgid ""
"Startup parameter values can be set when running the node through the ROS "
"launch facility. For information on how to specify parameters via launch, "
"see :doc:`../../Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-ROS2-Launch-For-Large-Projects`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:95
msgid "Setting initial parameter values when running a node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:97
msgid ""
"Initial parameter values can be set when running the node either through "
"individual command-line arguments, or through YAML files. "
"See :ref:`NodeArgsParameters` for examples on how to set initial parameter "
"values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:101
msgid "Manipulating parameter values at runtime"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:103
msgid ""
"The ``ros2 param`` command is the primary way to interact with parameters "
"for nodes that are already running. ``ros2 param`` uses the parameter "
"service API to perform the various operations. For details on how to use "
"``ros2 param``, see :doc:`Working-with-parameters/Using-ros2-param`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:107
msgid ""
"In addition to the command-line interface, parameters can also be "
"manipulated programmatically at runtime using ROS client libraries. All "
"client libraries provide APIs to get, set, and react to parameter changes "
"while a node is running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:111
msgid "Setting parameter callbacks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:113
msgid ""
"A ROS node can register callbacks to be informed when changes are happening "
"to parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:115
msgid ""
"For a demo example of these callbacks in use, see "
"`set_parameters_callback.cpp <https://github.com/ros2/demos/blob/rolling/"
"demo_nodes_cpp/src/parameters/set_parameters_callback.cpp>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:118
msgid "Pre-set parameter callbacks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:120
msgid ""
"*Pre-set parameter* callbacks can be set by calling "
"``add_pre_set_parameters_callback`` from the node API. This callback is "
"passed a list of the ``Parameter`` objects that are being changed, and "
"returns nothing. When it is called, it can modify the ``Parameter`` list to "
"change, add, or remove entries. For example, if ``parameter2`` should change "
"anytime that ``parameter1`` changes, that can be implemented with this "
"callback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:126
msgid "Set parameter callbacks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:128
msgid ""
"*Set parameter* callbacks can be set by calling "
"``add_on_set_parameters_callback`` from the node API. The callback is passed "
"a list of immutable ``Parameter`` objects, and returns an ``rcl_interfaces/"
"msg/SetParametersResult``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:132
msgid ""
"It is important that *set parameter* callbacks have no side-effects. Because "
"multiple *set parameter* callbacks can be chained, there is no way for an "
"individual callback to know if a later callback will reject the update. If "
"the individual callback were to make changes to the class it is in, for "
"example, it could get out-of-sync with the actual parameter. To get a "
"callback *after* a parameter has been successfully changed, use a post-set "
"parameter callback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:138
msgid "Post-set parameter callbacks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters.rst:140
msgid ""
"*Post-set parameter* callbacks can be set by calling "
"``add_post_set_parameters_callback`` from the node API. The callback is "
"passed a list of immutable ``Parameter`` objects, and returns nothing."
msgstr ""
